commits.message:
Server side:
1) Small domain fixes;
2) Transactional annotations;
3) Logging;

Client side:
1) Started statement summary controller;
2) Domain objects for statement entity completed;

Gigantic remodeling after last financial inspection of the condominium finances.

1) The aggregate root is Monthly Balance now, not apartment;
2) Domain packages were remodeled;
3) Previously implemented apartments page was removed. Will start with summary page now;
4) Lots of visual features, like:
 4.1) growl messages when a remote request is performed and when result is returned (success or failure);
 4.2) Spinning animated gif appears every time a remote request to the API is performed;
 4.3) Internationalization (i18n) with flag dropdown;
 4.4) No more Spring default favicon;
 4.5) Better background image;
 5) Improvements in the Lazy Collection Nullifier. Now it goes up in the hierarchy tree checking for collection properties;
 6) Lots of class renaming

Check Astah UML diagram

1) Repositories extend from JpaRespository and no longer from CrudRepository (want to deal with lists, not iterables);
2) Created service class to handle transactional operations;
3) Implemented GET api method (for testing purposes);
4) Web client structure using AngularJS is ready and accessing the Api using REST;
5) Spring security demands login and password directly from the browser;

First classes can be persisted!

Database:
1) Vagrant VM;
2) MySQL 5.5 provisioning;
3) Using MySQL Workbench;

Java:
1) Spring Boot JPA with application.properties file;
2) No repository implementation, only CrudRepsoitory extended interface;
3) Personalized interface operation using CrudRepository and @Query annotation;
4) Transactional and non transactional unit tests methods;
5) No use of @Autowired, only @Inject annotation;
6) Javax validator @NotNull using Hibernate validator provider;
7) Entities with unidirectional Many to Many relationship (based on DDD);
8) @Version in entities. Found out that they cannot be null from the beginning or NullPointerException will be thrown;
